  "prefLabel": "Emp 207.18 Role of Complainants in Enforcement or Disciplinary Hearings",
  "priorExpiration": "2008-10-17",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Emp 207.18 Role of Complainants in Enforcement or Disciplinary Hearings. Unless called as a witness or a party, a person who initiates an adjudicative proceeding by complaining to the department about the conduct of a person who becomes a party shall have no role in any enforcement or disciplinary hearing.\n\nSource. #7246, eff 4-30-00; ss by #9126, INTERIM, eff 4-20-08, EXPIRES: 10-17-08; ss by #9296, eff 10-17-08",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/emp100-500.html"
